   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: Transmission line infrastructure and Substation for transmitting power up to 3,700 MW had been completed. Due to overall investments in the state, Rajasthan achieved transmission network capacity to transmit 8,800 MW by 2018. Institutional capacity has been developed in RRVPNL to operate high-penetration solar and wind power generation in Rajasthan after implementing several transmission projects to evacuate renewable energy projects. Institutional capacity enhanced through TA implementation. The intended outcome under tranche 1 has been successfully achieved and over 9,000 MW of wind and solar capacity has been added resulting in GHG savings of 5.6 million tons per year.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
